@startuml Monitor Chiller Status Sequence Diagram
title Figure X: Sprint 1 — Monitor Chiller Status Sequence Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "Dashboard / Fault UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "ChillerOptimizer" as Optimizer <<Control>>
participant "Diagnostic Engine" as Engine <<Control>>
participant "ML Model API" as ML <<External Service>>
database "Supabase" as DB <<Database>>

== Real-Time Status Monitoring ==
autonumber
User -> UI : Open Dashboard
activate UI

UI -> DB : getOptimizationHistory()
activate DB
DB --> UI : recent history data
deactivate DB

UI -> Optimizer : calculateSavings(current_inputs)
activate Optimizer
Optimizer -> ML : POST features (Current Baseline)
activate ML
ML --> Optimizer : current efficiency (kW/ton)
deactivate ML
Optimizer --> UI : Baseline Performance Metrics
deactivate Optimizer

UI -> UI : Update SystemStatusCard
note right: Display: Chillers Running,\nEfficiency (kW/ton),\nActive Fault Count

== Manual Diagnostic Scan ==
User -> UI : Navigate to Fault Detection
User -> UI : Click "Run Full Diagnostics Scan"

UI -> Engine : runDiagnostics()
activate Engine
loop For each subsystem
    Engine -> Engine : Analyze Sensor Data Patterns
    Engine -> Engine : Calculate Anomaly Scores
end
Engine --> UI : Diagnostics Complete (List of Faults)
deactivate Engine

UI -> UI : Update Fault List & Health Metrics
UI --> User : Display Alerts & Anomaly Scores

@enduml
